course: dictionary
lesson: 2504
title: New word: debut
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A «debut» is the first time someone performs or appears in public, or the first time something new is shown to people. Writers use it when a singer, player or film is starting out and it is a big moment.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «Billie Eilish and her brother Finneas reportedly recorded much of her debut album on a computer in a small bedroom at home, and it won major awards.» The words «album» and «won major awards» tell you a debut album is the first album someone makes, and it can be a huge success.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "first" for debut: "much of her first album" still makes sense, so you have the right idea. A debut can also be a sports first, like «made his debut for England», which means he played for England for the very first time.
fact: Debut means the first time something happens, especially a first public appearance.
fact: «Debut» can be a noun or a verb: «a stunning debut» (noun), «the film will debut tonight» (verb).
fact: Phrases to learn: «make your debut», «debut album», «debut match».
fact: «Debut» is said "DAY-byoo" in English, and it comes from French, where it means a start or beginning.
fact: Use the clues in a sentence, such as «album» or «won awards», to check what a word means.
exercise: «Much of her debut album was recorded in a small bedroom.» What does debut mean here? | A cheap album sold in shops | Her last album before she stopped singing | Her first album | *Her first album, the first time it was released
exercise: «He made his debut for England.» What does this tell you? | *He played for England for the first time | He scored more goals than anyone ever | He was injured in training | He left the England team
exercise: «The new film will debut next month.» What does debut mean here? | Be sold at a cheaper price | Be made longer | Be cancelled before anyone sees it | *Be shown to the public for the first time
test: Ella reads «a stunning debut» in a music magazine. What does it mean? | A stunning view of the stage | A quiet start to a song | *An amazing first appearance | A debut is a kind of guitar
test: In the sentence «The band will debut tonight», what kind of word is debut? | An adjective | A pronoun | *A verb | A noun
exam: Ruby says a debut is the last time someone performs. What is the correct meaning? | *The first time someone performs or appears in public | A song that is played again and again | The final show before a long break | A quiet practice before a big show
